# AQP RL

- `aqp_rl/` owns the RL subsystem (spec, runtime, registry, core
  abstractions, component libraries, advantage estimators, policy
  backbones, weight-centric portfolio pipeline, Iceberg trajectory
  store, Celery task wrapper, FastAPI route, YAML spec library, tests).
- `aqp/rl/` is **compatibility shims only** — `aqp/rl/__init__.py`
  re-exports `aqp_rl.*` with `DeprecationWarning`. Do not add new
  source files under `aqp/rl/`.
- All RL train / evaluate / paper / replay / walk-forward go through
  [`RLRuntime`](mdc:aqp_rl/src/aqp_rl/runtime.py). Celery tasks
  ([`aqp_rl/tasks/rl_tasks.py`](mdc:aqp_rl/tasks/rl_tasks.py)) and the
  REST router
  ([`aqp_rl/api/routes/rl.py`](mdc:aqp_rl/api/routes/rl.py)) wrap it —
  never call `agent.train` directly.
- `rl_experiment_versions` rows are immutable, hash-locked snapshots.
  Re-snapshotting via
  [`registry.persist_spec`](mdc:aqp_rl/src/aqp_rl/registry.py) inserts
  a new version row when the SHA-256 hash changes.
- Every concrete RL component registers via the
  [`RLComponent`](mdc:aqp_rl/src/aqp_rl/core/base.py) metaclass. Set
  `rl_kind` (one of `rl_env`, `rl_reward`, `rl_observation`,
  `rl_action`, `rl_termination`, `rl_policy`, `rl_agent`, `rl_data`,
  `rl_ensembler`, `rl_experiment`, `rl_advantage_estimator`,
  `rl_policy_backbone`, `rl_trajectory_store`) and `rl_alias`.
  Don't decorate with `@register` manually.
- All trajectory / equity-curve / action-log / reward-decomposition
  writes go through
  [`IcebergTrajectoryStore`](mdc:aqp_rl/src/aqp_rl/trajectories/iceberg_writer.py)
  → `iceberg_catalog.append_arrow`. Never call PyIceberg directly.
- LLM calls inside `LLMHybridAgent` route through `router_complete`
  (in the monolith at
  [`aqp/llm/providers/router.py`](mdc:aqp/llm/providers/router.py)).
  No direct `litellm.completion` / `OllamaClient` from RL code.
- All weight-centric portfolio actions go through the four-stage
  pipeline `f_S -> f_A -> f_T -> f_R` in
  [`aqp_rl/src/aqp_rl/portfolio/pipeline.py`](mdc:aqp_rl/src/aqp_rl/portfolio/pipeline.py).
  The risk overlay (`f_R`) re-uses `RiskLimits` +
  `TargetWeightsRebalancer` from the monolith so offline backtest and
  live paper-trading produce identical target-weight vectors.

Validation:

```bash
cd aqp_rl
pip install -e .
pytest -ra
ruff check src tests
```
